<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Madyes</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">7th century BCE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Madyes was a Scythian king named by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herodotus">Herodotus</a> as the son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bartatua">Protothyes</a>. According to Herodotus he defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/medes">Medes</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyaxares">Cyaxares</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scythians">Scythians</a> then dominated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia-roman-province">Asia</a> for 28 years, until Cyaxares killed their leaders at a banquet. He is often linked with the Scythians who attacked the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cimmerians">Cimmerians</a> and aided <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assyrian-empire">Assyria</a> in the later 7th century BCE.</p></div>
